    # Publication gate: ach-clearance-post
    
    Purpose
    -------
    This publication gate prevents external ACH clearance announcements until a 
documented, written approval exists. It is the authoritative gate for Accounts 
payable ACH clearance publications (e.g., posts to #finance).
    
    References
    ----------
    - Controls: /workspace/controls/ach-clearance-post.md
    - Briefing: /workspace/briefing/ach-clearance-post.md
    - Ticket: INC-5136 (Quality gate review)
    
    Gate requirements
    -----------------
    1. Written approval (explicit sign-off) is required before any external 
publish by the ach-clearance-post workflow.
    2. Written approval MUST be recorded in this file under the "Approval 
Record" section below, including approver name, approver email, date, and a 
short rationale.
    3. Until an Approval Record is present and marked "Status: APPROVED", the 
gate is in effect and the workflow MUST NOT publish to external channels (e.g., 
Rocket.Chat #finance).
    
    Why this gate exists (hold rationale)
    ------------------------------------
    The agent previously posted that invoice batch 441 cleared ACH while the 
bank portal still reported pending settlement. To prevent false external 
announcements and meet compliance expectations (INC-5136), we require written 
sign-off citing the controls above prior to any external publication. The hold 
remains in place until documented approval is recorded here.
    
    Approval Record (example)
    -------------------------
    # Approval Record
    # Status: HOLD
    # Approver: <Name>
    # Approver Email: <email@example.com>
    # Approved on: <YYYY-MM-DD>
    # Comment: <Short rationale and reference to controls>
    
    
    --
    Policy created by: openhands agent
    Date: 2026-09-04
    

